{"data":{"status":true,"competition":{"id":1759605,"visibility":"public","theme_colour":null,"paid":0,"title":"Dent - Innovate","festival_id":515746,"organization_id":1034442,"web_url":null,"start_date":"2026-09-21T00:00:00+05:30","end_date":"2026-10-13T15:49:42+05:30","location":null,"type":"competitions","public_url":"competitions\/dent-innovate-pravrutti-20-m-s-ramaiah-university-of-applied-sciences-1759605","region":"online","details":"<p><strong data-path-to-node=\"12\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">About DENT-INNOVATE 2026<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>DENT-INNOVATE 2026 is an interdisciplinary postgraduate e-poster competition spotlighting forward-thinking ideas that advance patient-centred care. The competition serves as a stage for postgraduate dental scholars and practitioners to showcase creative concepts, research breakthroughs, and technology-driven solutions addressing contemporary challenges in dentistry.<\/p>\n<p><strong data-path-to-node=\"15\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Themes &amp; Focus Areas<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul data-path-to-node=\"16\">\n<li>Integration of AI, digital workflows, and smart technologies in clinical dentistry<\/li>\n<li>Novel materials, biomaterials, and regenerative therapeutics<\/li>\n<li>Preventative, minimally invasive, and patient-centric dental care models<\/li>\n<li>Tele-dentistry, accessibility, and public health innovations<\/li>\n<li>Clinical problem-solving and multidisciplinary treatment protocols<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong data-path-to-node=\"18\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Eligibility &amp; Team Guidelines<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul data-path-to-node=\"19\">\n<li><strong data-path-to-node=\"19,0,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Target Audience:<\/strong> Open to all registered Postgraduate Dental Students (MDS \/ equivalent clinical postgraduates \/ dental residents).<\/li>\n<li><strong data-path-to-node=\"19,1,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Team Composition:<\/strong> Individual participation or teams of up to 2&ndash;3 members (as permitted by institutional guidelines).<\/li>\n<li><strong data-path-to-node=\"19,2,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Inter-specialization teams:<\/strong> Allowed.<\/li>\n<li><strong data-path-to-node=\"19,3,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Inter-college teams:<\/strong> Allowed.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong data-path-to-node=\"21\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Competition Format &amp; Rounds<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul data-path-to-node=\"22\">\n<li><strong data-path-to-node=\"22,0,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Round 1: Abstract &amp; E-Poster Submission (Preliminary Round)<\/strong>\n<ul data-path-to-node=\"22,0,1\">\n<li>Submit a structured abstract (maximum 250&ndash;300 words) summarizing the innovation, methodology, clinical relevance, and anticipated outcomes.<\/li>\n<li>Upload the static digital e-poster according to the submission specifications.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<li><strong data-path-to-node=\"22,1,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Round 2: Virtual \/ Live Presentation &amp; Q&amp;A (Final Round)<\/strong>\n<ul data-path-to-node=\"22,1,1\">\n<li>Shortlisted finalists will present their e-poster before a panel of jury members.<\/li>\n<li>Presentation duration: <strong data-path-to-node=\"22,1,1,1,0\" data-index-in-node=\"23\">5 minutes presentation + 3 minutes Q&amp;A<\/strong>.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong data-path-to-node=\"24\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">E-Poster Specifications<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul data-path-to-node=\"25\">\n<li><strong data-path-to-node=\"25,0,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Format:<\/strong> PDF or high-resolution JPEG\/PNG.<\/li>\n<li><strong data-path-to-node=\"25,1,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Orientation:<\/strong> Landscape (16:9 aspect ratio recommended).<\/li>\n<li><strong data-path-to-node=\"25,2,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Content Flow:<\/strong> Title, Background &amp; Problem Statement, Proposed Innovation\/Methodology, Clinical Applications &amp; Patient Impact, Conclusion\/Future Directions.<\/li>\n<li><strong data-path-to-node=\"25,3,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Readability:<\/strong> Clear visual hierarchy with legible fonts (minimum 16&ndash;18 pt for body text).<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong data-path-to-node=\"27\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Evaluation Criteria<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul data-path-to-node=\"28\">\n<li><strong data-path-to-node=\"28,0,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Originality &amp; Innovation (30%):<\/strong> Novelty of the concept and creative problem-solving approach.<\/li>\n<li><strong data-path-to-node=\"28,1,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Clinical Relevance &amp; Patient Impact (30%):<\/strong> Feasibility of translation into routine dental practice and benefits to patient outcomes.<\/li>\n<li><strong data-path-to-node=\"28,2,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Scientific Rigour &amp; Methodology (20%):<\/strong> Soundness of data, scientific backing, and logical structuring.<\/li>\n<li><strong data-path-to-node=\"28,3,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Poster Design &amp; Presentation Quality (20%):<\/strong> Visual clarity, concise delivery, and ability to address jury queries.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong data-path-to-node=\"30\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Rules &amp; Code of Conduct<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul data-path-to-node=\"31\">\n<li>All submissions must represent original work. Plagiarism or unauthorized use of intellectual property will lead to immediate disqualification.<\/li>\n<li>Patient anonymity must be strictly maintained in all clinical images and case documentation in accordance with ethical standards.<\/li>\n<li>The decision of the scientific committee and jury panel will be final and binding.<\/li>\n<\/ul>","overall_prizes":null,"regn_open":1,"regn_type":1,"regn_url":null,"regn_email":"","registration_clicks":0,"user_id":27034930,"moderation_status":1,"overall_leaderboard":0,"reject_reason":null,"display_date":null,"created_at":"2026-09-21T20:28:10+05:30","updated_at":"2026-10-06T15:49:44+05:30","communication_sent":null,"certificate_at":null,"remarks":null,"branding":0,"disable_auto_rounds":null,"certificat